From 5f9c3ef93b7b066a4bcec75a3a82c215b2b9beaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Donovici <azerty10997@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:49:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: NEON smmla GEMM and sdot GEMV for iq4_xs_8x8_q8_K

The GEMM feeds vmmlaq_s32 directly: a 16-byte weight load (one column pair)
meets a 16-byte activation load (one row pair) with no shuffling, since the
interleaved layout already stores 8 bytes per column contiguously. Lanes 0-1
carry the first column's scale and 2-3 the second's, so the scale vector is
[s0, s0, s1, s1]. IQ4_XS needs one 6-bit scale per 32-element sub-block and no
min term, which makes this materially simpler than the q4_K equivalent.

The GEMV stays on DOTPROD: at nr == 1 there is no second activation row to fill
an smmla operand, and regressing batch-1 decode off the existing vec_dot path
would cost more than the prefill win is worth. Activations are loaded once per
8-element run and duplicated so one vdotq serves both columns of a pair.

Validated against the non-repacked path across gemv-only, gemm-only and mixed
shapes: max_abs 3.8e-06, below both the portable reference (1.5e-05) and
upstream's own q4_K repack kernel (1.1e-05), as smmla accumulates exactly in
int32 with fewer float rounding steps.
